# obs_key_from_virtual_key (keysym -> obs key): linear search of the keysym table copied from the server for the FIRST
# matching entry; the keycode is min_keycode + index/syms_per_code; the result is the obs key owning that keycode (so a SHIFTED
# keysym such as '!' resolves to the key of the physical key, here OBS_KEY_1). 0 -> NONE; unknown -> NONE; a keycode that
# no obs key claimed -> NONE. obs_key_to_virtual_key: META -> Super_L, otherwise the base keysym (0 when none).
x11_setup 8 40 4
x11_map 10 XK_1 XK_exclam
x11_map 11 XK_a XK_A
x11_map 15 XK_Super_L
x11_map 17 XK_Return
x11_map 30 XK_Hyper_L
hk_init
hk_from_vk XK_1
hk_from_vk XK_exclam
hk_from_vk XK_a
hk_from_vk XK_A
hk_from_vk XK_Return
hk_from_vk XK_Super_L
hk_from_vk XK_Hyper_L
hk_from_vk 0
hk_from_vk 0x12345678
hk_to_vk OBS_KEY_A
hk_to_vk OBS_KEY_META
hk_to_vk OBS_KEY_RETURN
hk_to_vk OBS_KEY_NONE
hk_to_vk OBS_KEY_MOUSE1
hk_to_vk OBS_KEY_F1
hk_free
